{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויעש בצלאל את הארון", :translit "va'ya'as betzalel et ha'aron", :gloss "and made Bezalel the ark"} {:he "בכולם לא הזכיר בצלאל", :translit "be'kulam lo hizkir betzalel", :gloss "in all of them he did not mention Bezalel"} {:he "סוד הארון והמרכבה", :translit "sod ha'aron ve'ha'merkavah", :gloss "the secret of the ark and the Chariot"} {:he "הארון הוא כנגד כסא הכבוד", :translit "ha'aron hu ke'neged kis'e ha'kavod", :gloss "the ark is opposite the Throne of Glory"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Literary observation: Bezalel is named only for the ark among all the Tabernacle furnishings"}], :frame {:text "The Ark is identified with the Throne of Glory: its cherubim are the source for calling God 'He who sits [above] the cherubim' (1 Samuel 4:4; 2 Kings 19:15). Ezekiel chapter 1 describes the divine Chariot (merkavah), a vision of the heavenly realm. The Talmud states that Bezalel was endowed with wisdom to combine letters through which heaven and earth were created (Berakhot 55a).", :sources ["1 Samuel 4:4" "2 Kings 19:15" "Ezekiel 1" "Berakhot 55a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Literary observation: Bezalel is named only for the ark among all the Tabernacle furnishings", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:21:15.127249351Z", :model "glm-5.2"}